---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = 'November 11, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="Oropis privacy policy.">
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: {updated}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap narrow prose">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>Oropis uses cookies for two things: aggregate analytics and advertising. Non-essential cookies are off unless you accept them, and you can change your choice at any time with the <strong>Cookie settings</strong> link in the footer. We do not sell personal data.</p>

    <h2>What the site collects</h2>
    <p>The public site is a static website served by GitHub Pages. Our hosting provider may process standard request data such as IP address, user agent, and requested URL to deliver and protect the site. Oropis does not receive or maintain a reader database from that traffic.</p>

    <h2>Cookies, analytics, and advertising</h2>
    <p><strong>Analytics.</strong> We use Google Analytics 4 to understand which stories are read and how readers find us. Analytics cookies are set only if you accept non-essential cookies.</p>
    <p><strong>Advertising.</strong> We use Google AdSense to display ads. AdSense and its partners may use cookies to serve and measure ads. If you reject non-essential cookies, ads may still appear but will not be personalized.</p>
    <p><strong>Your choice.</strong> Non-essential cookies are denied by default. Accepting or rejecting them applies to both analytics and advertising. Use the <strong>Cookie settings</strong> link in the footer to make or change your choice.</p>
    <p>For details on how Google handles data, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google's Privacy &amp; Terms</a>.</p>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>If you email the desk, we receive your address and message. We use them to respond and, where relevant, to verify a tip or correction. We do not add correspondents to a marketing list.</p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>Stories link to primary sources and other sites. Those sites have their own privacy practices. Embedded media is not used at launch; hero images are cached locally with credit.</p>

    <h2>Search</h2>
    <p>Site search runs in your browser against a static index. Search queries are not sent to an Oropis server.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:abhishek.shinde@oropis.com">abhishek.shinde@oropis.com</a>.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
